# Copy this file to .env and paste your key in.
#
#   macOS / Linux:  cp .env.example .env
#   Windows:        copy .env.example .env
#
# .env is listed in .gitignore, so it never reaches GitHub.
# Never paste your key into your code, your README, a screenshot, or a message.
# If you think you've exposed it, say so in the help channel and delete the
# key — keys are free to replace and nobody is in trouble for it.
#
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com — sign in with a Google
# account, CREATE YOUR OWN PROJECT when prompted, and make a key inside it.
# The free quota is counted per project. Two students sharing one project
# split one student's allowance.

GEMINI_API_KEY=""
# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# You shouldn't need these. They're here so you can change behaviour without
# editing config.py.

# Which corpus to use. See corpora/README.md.
# AI201_CORPUS=campus_life

# Turn the response cache off entirely (evaluation runs already do this).
# AI201_CACHE=0
